# Example crontab entry for pm25-flipboard.
# Edit your crontab with:  crontab -e     (list it with: crontab -l)
#
# Fields: minute  hour  day-of-month  month  day-of-week  command
#
# Run every 30 minutes (at :00 and :30), only between 07:00 and 22:59 local time,
# so the board stays quiet overnight. Cron uses wall-clock times, not time since boot.
#
# Replace the two paths below:
#   - the Python interpreter  (find yours with: which python3)
#   - the script              (use the FULL path; cron does not start in your folder)
#
# Output (and any errors) are appended to a log in your home folder. /tmp also
# works but is cleared on reboot on many systems.

*/30 7-22 * * * /usr/bin/python3 /home/YOUR_USER/pm25-flipboard/code/purpleair_to_vestaboard_datetime.py >> $HOME/aq_vestaboard.log 2>&1

# To pause this job, put a # at the start of the line above.
# On macOS, a script inside ~/Documents, ~/Desktop or ~/Downloads may be blocked
# ("Operation not permitted"); keep it somewhere else under your home folder.
